'''Derreck Lamar Robinson''' (March 3, 1982 – August 2025) was an American professional [[American football|football]] player who was a [[defensive end]] in the [[National Football League]] (NFL). He played [[college football]] for the [[Iowa Hawkeyes football|Iowa Hawkeyes]] and was signed by the [[San Diego Chargers]] as an [[undrafted free agent]] in 2005. 

Robinson was also a member of the [[Miami Dolphins]], [[Dallas Cowboys]], and [[Cleveland Browns]]. He died in [[San Diego|San Diego, California]], in August 2025, at the age of 43.<ref>{{cite news |last1=Harty |first1=Pat |title=Former Iowa defensive lineman Derreck Robinson passes away at 43 |url=https://hawkfanatic.com/2025/08/13/former-iowa-defensive-lineman-derreck-robinson-passes-away-at-43/ |access-date=13 August 2025 |publisher=Hawk Fanatic |date=13 August 2025}}</ref>
